WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.846
Search the saved public road in The Gap, Brisbane. The example uses surveyed building outlines and bare-earth elevations.

00:00:03.846 --> 00:00:07.327
The 350 m radius contains 417 mapped footprints. The aerial photo is from 2022 and the LiDAR survey from 2019.

00:00:07.327 --> 00:00:11.002
Inspect a footprint, then select NE to compare the three upwind bands.

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:15.309
NE has 8, 17 and 49 mapped buildings. Their density and available heights suggest TC3 in all three viewing bands.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:19.895
Change to north. The ground profile crosses the site at 52.9 m AHD. The highest sampled point is 72.9 m to the south.

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:24.906
On the east–west profile the site lies on a slope. The engineer reviews the terrain and assesses Mt before applying it to wind pressure.
